To enable loading the crash kernel, append crashkernel=128M to the
Linux command line.

By default, crash dumping will use the default initrd and dump in
runit stage 1 to /var/crash.

You can place a custom initrd used for crash dumping as
/boot/initramfs-${KERNELVERSION}kdump.img.

On Sunlight (slinit as PID 1) the same work is done by the kdump slinit
service, which the package enables: it saves the dump before local.target
and then reboots with `slinitctl shutdown reboot`. Disable it with
`slinitctl disable kdump`; boot with nokdump to skip one dump.
